window.MAHA_DATA={"version":5,"text":{"heroEyebrow":"FOR THE STORIES NOT YET TOLD. THE IDEAS NOT YET MADE.","heroLine":"SHASHIKUMARA","heroItalic":"RENUKAPRASADA HUGARA","heroNote":"Some thoughts become stories. Some become experiences. I follow the ones that refuse to leave.","originTitle":"A little restless.\nA lot of wonder.","originBody":"I notice the story inside a silence, the possibility inside a question, and the world inside a passing thought. Then I try to give it a shape someone else can feel.","originSecond":"Words are where I wander. Design is how I make an idea visible. Curiosity is what keeps every door open. This is a collection of the things I am making, imagining, and still becoming.","workTitle":"NOT ALL WORLDS\nBEGIN WITH A MAP.","workIntro":"Some begin with a question. Others with a feeling. Step inside the work and follow what happened next.","writingTitle":"STAY A LITTLE.\nFEEL A LITTLE MORE.","writingBody":"The laughter before the chaos. The courage after the loss. The love that changes the shape of everything. Stories begin where life becomes impossible to ignore.","contactTitle":"BRING THE IDEA\nTHAT WON’T LET GO.","contactBody":"Bring a question, a rough sketch, or a story you cannot stop thinking about. Let us give it somewhere to go."},"theme":{"ink":"#1e2a28","cream":"#f4efdf","accent":"#df8a0d","moss":"#73ad87","font":"editorial"},"images":{"portrait":"assets/about-preview.webp","canopy":"assets/canopy.webp","waves":"assets/blue-waves.webp","sun":"assets/blue-circle-transparent.webp","green":"assets/green-contours.webp","yellow":"assets/yellow-lines.webp","purple":"assets/purple-contours.webp","entranceScene":"assets/entrance-supplied-laptop.webp","entranceMobile":"assets/entrance-supplied-mobile.webp","entranceTablet":"assets/entrance-supplied-tablet.webp","categoryCanopy":"assets/canopy-final.webp"},"sections":["origin","portals","featured","writing","gallery","contact"],"hidden":[],"projects":[{"id":"echobound","title":"ECHOBOUND","realm":"product","label":"GAME DESIGN / PRODUCT STRATEGY","tagline":"The world remembers you.","image":"data:image/webp;base64,","status":"Independent product concept","description":"An Indian-inspired adventure game about the consequences of what we choose to restore. A Waykeeper enters a fractured valley, where one recovered component can reconnect an outpost or restart a workshop.","decision":"The first chapter concentrates the product promise into a single decision. Each branch changes a place, a character response, and an opportunity. A structured Echo system keeps those consequences consistent across saving and loading.","next":"The specification defines the first playable scope, player journeys, state rules, interfaces, acceptance criteria, planned research, and delivery gates. A released game and validated player outcomes are not claimed.","pdf":"assets/ECHOBOUND_Product_Project.pdf","externalUrl":"https://cozy-starburst-7d1b70.netlify.app/"},{"id":"flavour","title":"FLAVOUR QUEST","realm":"product","label":"FOOD / CULTURE / EXPERIENCE DESIGN","tagline":"Every flavour has a story.","image":"data:image/webp;base64,","status":"Independent product concept","description":"A culinary discovery experience that brings regional food stories into flexible neighbourhood trails. The proposed first pilot explores a small Mysuru cluster through food, culture, and the people behind them.","decision":"The living trail can adapt when a stop closes. A personal food passport separates stories read from visits and purchases. Reading never requires a paid meal, and clear information takes priority over decorative rewards.","next":"The project covers merchant operations, interface direction, dietary disclosures, offline behaviour, planned validation, pilot economics, and launch conditions. Routes, partners, and outcomes remain to be verified.","pdf":"assets/FLAVOUR_QUEST_Product_Project.pdf","externalUrl":"https://fascinating-flan-692846.netlify.app/"},{"id":"shreera","title":"Shreera Kalyana","realm":"writing","label":"NOVEL / LOVE / COMEDY","tagline":"Two villages. One wedding. A thousand things that could go wrong.","image":"data:image/webp;base64,","status":"Novel in development","description":"Ramana belongs to a village in North Karnataka. Shree comes from a forest-side home near the coast. Their wedding brings two worlds together in an affectionate collision of village pride, love, laughter, and unexpected danger.","decision":"The story grows through the people around the couple: communities that take responsibility for their children, rituals that bring everyone together, and chaos that tests how far that affection will carry them.","next":"An evolving fiction project. The complete manuscript is not published on this website."},{"id":"ranarangam","title":"Ranarangam","realm":"writing","label":"NOVEL / POLITICS / DRAMA","tagline":"A young hero. A larger stage. A harder question.","image":"data:image/webp;base64,","status":"Novel in development","description":"A college student’s instinct to stand up for others draws him into public life and political conflict. His journey toward becoming chief minister asks what happens to conviction when it meets power.","decision":"The creative focus is the distance between personal heroism and public responsibility: the decisions a person can make alone and the consequences a state must live with.","next":"A fiction project in development, presented here through its premise. still in writing","externalUrl":""},{"id":"losers","title":"Resident of Losers’ Paradise","realm":"writing","label":"BOOK CONCEPT / LIFE / FAILURE","tagline":"What remains when the victory never comes?","image":"data:image/webp;base64,","status":"Book concept in development","description":"A story built around lives that refuse the familiar promise of a final victory. Repeated setbacks become a way of exploring dignity, endurance, and the meanings people seek when success offers no explanation.","decision":"The central creative decision is to resist an easy redemptive ending and stay with the emotional truth of experiences that remain unresolved.","next":"A developing book concept. No publication or reader reception is claimed.","externalUrl":""},{"id":"contoso","title":"Ledger Sentinel","realm":"data","label":"SAP-Inspired Finance Exception Review","tagline":"An accounting review prototype that connects transaction checks, reconciliations, and financial report verification with supporting evidence.","image":"data:image/webp;base64,","status":"SAP-Inspired Finance Exception Review","description":"LedgerSentinel is a US accounting portfolio project I built to bring accounting controls, reconciliation, and report verification into one workspace. Using sample data, it flags issues such as unbalanced journals, missing approvals, possible duplicate payments, and intercompany differences. Users can investigate flagged items, examine supporting records, and export a review pack.","decision":"I wanted to explore a simple question: can every financial conclusion be traced back to clear evidence? LedgerSentinel grew from the idea that identifying a difference is only the beginning. A reviewer also needs to understand the records behind it, what remains unexplained, and whether the financial report reflects those findings.","next":"LedgerSentinel is a working portfolio prototype with a hosted interactive preview using synthetic accounting data. The preview demonstrates its checks and investigation workflow. Live AI assistance, data imports, and saved reviews require the local server. It remains a demonstration project that requires human judgment when reviewing findings.","externalUrl":"https://stunning-cobbler-ee7ad0.netlify.app/"},{"id":"accounting-reconcile","title":"Junior","label":"SAP-Inspired Finance Investigation","tagline":"Junior is a finance review prototype that helps investigate invoice discrepancies, payment blocks, bank matching issues, and cost allocation errors using supporting records.","image":"data:image/webp;base64,","description":"I built Junior as an independent portfolio project inspired by SAP FI, MM, and CO workflows. It compares purchase orders, invoices, and goods receipts, reassesses historical payment blocks, suggests possible bank matches, and checks cost allocation configurations. Using synthetic data, it connects each finding with the evidence needed for further review.","decision":"I wanted to make financial exceptions easier to understand and investigate. A blocked invoice, an unmatched payment, or an allocation error tells only part of the story. Junior brings the surrounding records together to explain why an issue exists, whether circumstances have changed, and what evidence is still needed before a decision can be made.","next":"I wanted to make financial exceptions easier to understand and investigate. A blocked invoice, an unmatched payment, or an allocation error tells only part of the story. Junior brings the surrounding records together to explain why an issue exists, whether circumstances have changed, and what evidence is still needed before a decision can be made.","realm":"accounting","status":"Working Prototype · Interactive Preview","externalUrl":"https://nimble-pixie-75cef1.netlify.app/"},{"id":"accounting-close","title":"Finance IQ","label":"MONTH-END CLOSE / BOOKKEEPING","tagline":"FinanceIQ is a financial analysis dashboard that brings month-end reporting, bank reconciliation, outstanding balances, and cash flow forecasting into one workspace.","image":"data:image/webp;base64,","description":"I built FinanceIQ to connect accounting review with financial planning. Using synthetic data from a fictional distribution business, it presents financial statements, budget comparisons, bank reconciliation exceptions, and receivables and payables ageing. Its interactive 13-week cash forecast lets users explore how collection delays, collection rates, and trading assumptions affect available cash.","decision":"Link each closing task to its supporting evidence. Review accruals, prepayments, depreciation, and reconciliations before preparing the final trial balance.","next":"Planned outputs: a close checklist, journal register, supporting schedules, and review notes.","realm":"accounting","status":"Working Prototype · Interactive Demo","externalUrl":"https://splendid-pudding-ae1312.netlify.app/"},{"id":"accounting-statements","title":"The Cost Behind the Circuit","label":"FINANCIAL STATEMENTS / ANALYSIS","tagline":"An independent research paper exploring how commodity price movements can affect manufacturing costs, profit margins, and working capital in Indian electronics manufacturing.","image":"data:image/webp;base64,","description":"An independent research paper exploring how commodity price movements can affect manufacturing costs, profit margins, and working capital in Indian electronics manufacturing.","decision":"Read ratios in context. Compare profitability, liquidity, working capital, and cash conversion, and distinguish the reported figures from interpretation.","next":"Planned outputs: linked statements, ratio workings, and an evidence-based commentary.","realm":"accounting","status":"Working Paper · Available to Read","externalUrl":"https://frabjous-conkies-5ac226.netlify.app/"},{"id":"blog-1","title":"The Fish and the Butterfly","realm":"blogs","label":"Short Fiction · Love & Human Connection","tagline":"A moving story of love, family pressure, and friendship, following two people whose quiet dreams of a shared life face a painful choice.","image":"data:image/webp;base64,","status":"Published on Medium","description":"The Fish and the Butterfly follows Manu and Aradhana as affection grows through playful conversations, thoughtful gifts, and everyday care. When family expectations threaten their relationship, the story explores separation, belonging, and the friendship that supports them. Recurring images of a fish and a butterfly connect their love with a fragile possibility of hope.","decision":"I explored how small acts of care can carry the meaning of an entire relationship. An elderly couple holding hands becomes an image of the future Aradhana wishes for, while the fish and butterfly express connection across different worlds. The story asks what happens when love meets expectations about family, money, and security.","next":"The completed story is published on Medium as part of my creative writing portfolio. Its ending leaves the future open, allowing the themes of love, friendship, and hope to stay with the reader.","externalUrl":"https://medium.com/@shashikumarrh9945/the-fish-and-the-butterfly-991eea4dc8ac"},{"id":"blog-2","title":"Whispers on the Rails: A Journey of Love and Destiny","realm":"blogs","label":"Creative Writing · Love & Destiny","tagline":"A story of love and destiny set against a railway journey, inviting readers into the possibilities of an unexpected connection.","image":"data:image/webp;base64,","status":"Published on Medium","description":"Whispers on the Rails is my creative storytelling piece exploring love and destiny through the setting of a train journey. It brings together the movement of travel and the emotional possibilities of people whose paths cross along the way.","decision":"A train brings different lives together for a brief stretch of time. That setting offers a powerful way to explore connection, uncertainty, and the possibility that an ordinary journey might become personally meaningful.","next":"The story is shared on Medium as part of my creative writing portfolio, reflecting my interest in love, human connection, and emotionally driven storytelling.","externalUrl":"https://medium.com/@shashikumarrh9945/whispers-on-the-rails-a-journey-of-love-and-destiny-d38657312a82"},{"id":"blog-3","title":"The Missing Rows: India’s Audit Risk Beyond the Ledger","realm":"blogs","label":"Audit Evidence & Data Completeness","tagline":"An open page for your next idea.","image":"data:image/webp;base64,","status":"Published Blog Article","description":"An analytical blog exploring how excluded transactions, incomplete data extracts, and gaps in audit trails can limit what an audit establishes.","decision":"I wanted to look beyond the accuracy of recorded numbers and question how the records were selected. Testing every row in a spreadsheet can sound comprehensive, but it leaves an important question unanswered: what was excluded? The article explores why understanding the boundaries of a dataset matters as much as analysing its contents.","next":"The article is published on my blog as an independent commentary on audit evidence and data completeness. It combines public regulatory observations, auditing principles, and clearly identified hypothetical examples. Its proposed documentation approach offers a practical point for discussion rather than a new auditing standard.","externalUrl":"https://shashikumarrh.blogspot.com/2026/10/the-missing-rows-indias-audit-risk.html"}]};
